    "tut_place_fw_title": "Deploy Firewall",
    "tut_place_fw_text": 'The <span class="text-purple-400 font-bold">Firewall</span> is your first line of defense. It blocks <span class="text-red-400">MALICIOUS</span> traffic (red) that can destroy your reputation. Click the FW button, then click on the grid to place it.',
    "tut_place_fw_hint": "Place the Firewall close to the Internet node (the cyan box on the left) for easier connection.",
    "tut_connect_fw_title": "Connect to Internet",
    "tut_connect_fw_text": 'Great! Now connect the <span class="text-cyan-400 font-bold">Internet</span> to your Firewall. Select the <span class="text-blue-400 font-bold">Link</span> tool, click on Internet first, then click on the Firewall.',
    "tut_connect_fw_hint": "All traffic enters through the Internet node. Without this connection, no traffic will reach your infrastructure.",
    "tut_place_lb_title": "Deploy Load Balancer",
    "tut_place_lb_text": 'The <span class="text-blue-400 font-bold">Load Balancer</span> distributes traffic across multiple servers. This prevents overload and improves reliability.',
    "tut_place_lb_hint": "Load Balancers use Round Robin to evenly distribute requests.",
    "tut_connect_fw_lb_title": "Connect Firewall to LB",
    "tut_connect_fw_lb_text": "Connect your Firewall to the Load Balancer. Clean traffic will flow from Firewall \u2192 Load Balancer.",
    "tut_connect_fw_lb_hint": "Traffic flow: Internet \u2192 Firewall (blocks MALICIOUS) \u2192 Load Balancer \u2192 ...",
    "tut_place_compute_title": "Deploy Compute Server",
    "tut_place_compute_text": '<span class="text-orange-400 font-bold">Compute</span> processes all requests. It routes traffic to the correct destination: <span class="text-emerald-400">Storage</span> for STATIC/UPLOAD, <span class="text-red-400">Database</span> for READ/WRITE/SEARCH.',
    "tut_place_compute_hint": "You can upgrade Compute later to handle more traffic (Tier 1 \u2192 2 \u2192 3). Heavy requests like UPLOAD and SEARCH take longer to process.",
    "tut_connect_lb_compute_title": "Connect LB to Compute",
    "tut_connect_lb_compute_text": "Connect the Load Balancer to your Compute server.",
    "tut_connect_lb_compute_hint": "You can add multiple Compute servers and the Load Balancer will distribute traffic between them.",
    "tut_place_storage_title": "Deploy File Storage",
    "tut_place_storage_text": '<span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold">File Storage</span> handles <span class="text-green-400">STATIC</span> (green) and <span class="text-yellow-400">UPLOAD</span> (yellow) traffic. Without it, these requests will fail!',
    "tut_place_storage_hint": "STATIC = images, CSS, JS files (90% cache hit rate). UPLOAD = file uploads (heavy, never cached).",
    "tut_place_cdn_title": "Deploy CDN",
    "tut_place_cdn_text": '<span class="text-green-400 font-bold">CDN</span> (Content Delivery Network) speeds up <span class="text-green-400">STATIC</span> content delivery. It sits between the Internet and Storage.',
    "tut_place_cdn_hint": "CDNs have a very high cache hit rate (95%), meaning most requests never need to touch your Storage servers!",
    "tut_connect_internet_cdn_title": "Connect Internet to CDN",
    "tut_connect_internet_cdn_text": 'Connect the <span class="text-cyan-400 font-bold">Internet</span> to your <span class="text-green-400 font-bold">CDN</span>. This allows users to hit the edge cache first.',
    "tut_connect_internet_cdn_hint": "Traffic flow: Internet \u2192 CDN. If cache miss \u2192 Storage.",
    "tut_connect_cdn_s3_title": "Connect CDN to Storage",
    "tut_connect_cdn_s3_text": 'Connect the <span class="text-green-400 font-bold">CDN</span> to <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold">File Storage</span>. This allows the CDN to fetch content on cache misses.',
    "tut_connect_cdn_s3_hint": "Only cache misses (5%) will go to Storage. This saves money and capacity!",
    "tut_place_db_title": "Deploy SQL Database",
    "tut_place_db_text": '<span class="text-red-400 font-bold">SQL Database</span> handles <span class="text-blue-400">READ</span>, <span class="text-orange-400">WRITE</span>, and <span class="text-cyan-400">SEARCH</span> traffic. APIs need database storage.',
    "tut_place_db_hint": "READ = data fetch (40% cache). WRITE = database updates (never cached). SEARCH = complex queries (15% cache, heavy).",
    "tut_connect_compute_storage_title": "Connect to Storage",
    "tut_connect_compute_storage_text": 'Connect <span class="text-orange-400">Compute</span> to <span class="text-emerald-400">File Storage</span>. Use the Link tool.',
    "tut_connect_compute_storage_hint": "Compute automatically routes STATIC and UPLOAD traffic to File Storage.",
    "tut_connect_compute_db_title": "Connect to Database",
    "tut_connect_compute_db_text": 'Connect <span class="text-orange-400">Compute</span> to <span class="text-red-400">SQL Database</span>.',
    "tut_connect_compute_db_hint": "Compute automatically routes READ, WRITE, and SEARCH traffic to SQL Database.",
    "tut_ready_title": "Infrastructure Ready!",
    "tut_ready_text": 'Your basic infrastructure is complete! Press the <span class="text-green-400 font-bold">Play</span> button to start the simulation. Watch as traffic flows through your system!',
    "tut_ready_hint": "Monitor the colored rings around services - green is good, red means overload. Upgrade or add more services as needed!",
    "tut_complete_title": "Tutorial Complete!",
    "tut_complete_text": `<span class="text-green-400">Congratulations!</span> You now know the basics. Remember:<br><br>\u2022 <span class="text-red-400">Red</span> MALICIOUS \u2192 Block with Firewall<br>\u2022 <span class="text-green-400">Green</span> STATIC / <span class="text-yellow-400">Yellow</span> UPLOAD \u2192 Route to Storage<br>\u2022 <span class="text-blue-400">Blue</span> READ / <span class="text-orange-400">Orange</span> WRITE \u2192 Route to <span class="text-violet-400">NoSQL DB</span> (fast) or SQL DB<br>\u2022 <span class="text-cyan-400">Cyan</span> SEARCH \u2192 Route to SQL DB only (NoSQL can't handle SEARCH)<br>\u2022 <span class="text-fuchsia-400">API Gateway</span> rate limits traffic \u2014 throttled requests lose less reputation<br>\u2022 Cache helps STATIC (90%), READ (40%), SEARCH (15%)<br><br>Good luck, Architect!`,
    "tut_complete_hint": "Don't worry if your budget goes negative at first! Just like real infrastructure - you invest upfront, then profit comes from processed traffic. Each completed request earns money!",
    "tut_start_playing": "Start Playing!",
